    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": " How is this different from melatonin?",
            "answer": "<p>Melatonin sends the circadian sleep signal it tells your brain it is time for bed. L-Theanine reduces the cognitive overactivation that prevents sleep onset the racing thoughts and wired-but-tired feeling that keeps you awake even when you are exhausted.</p><p>They address completely different mechanisms and are complementary, not interchangeable. If you are lying awake with your mind running, the problem may not be your circadian signal. It may be excess glutamate keeping your brain active when it should be quieting down.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take this during the day without getting drowsy?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, that is one of L-Theanine's defining properties. At 200mg, it induces measurable alpha brain wave activity the neural state of relaxed, focused alertness without causing sedation or cognitive impairment.</p><p>Many users take it specifically with morning coffee: L-Theanine at 200mg paired with standard caffeine intake smooths the jittery, anxious edge of caffeine while maintaining alertness and focus. This is the most clinically studied use case for L-Theanine in productivity contexts.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the right time to take it morning or night?",
            "answer": "<p>Both, depending on your goal. For calm focus and caffeine synergy: after your morning meal, with or just after coffee. For pre-sleep cognitive quiet: 30-45 minutes before bed.</p><p>One capsule per day covers most people. Some individuals take it both morning and night consult your healthcare professional if you want to increase your dose.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this the same amino acid found in green tea?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. L-Theanine is found almost exclusively in the leaves of Camellia sinensis the tea plant. It is the compound responsible for the distinct calm-focused state that distinguishes matcha and high-quality green tea from coffee, despite both containing caffeine.</p><p>AIWO L-Theanine delivers the same amino acid in a consistent, measured 200mg dose per capsule the clinically studied amount for alpha wave induction</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WyBt4K": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I notice an effect?",
            "answer": "<p>L-Theanine has a rapid onset relative to most supplements: alpha wave changes are measurable on EEG within 30-45 minutes of a 200mg dose in fasted or post-meal conditions. Subjective effects reduced mental tension, increased cognitive clarity are typically noticeable within the same window for most users.</p><p>For cumulative benefits (consistent stress resilience, improved sleep quality), continued daily use over 4-8 weeks provides the most reliable results. Individual results vary.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_item_BFc6Am",
